{"record_kind": "BaseDuty", "meaning": "A volunteer's duty at a base over an interval. `duty` is the capacity
they served in then, not a lasting trait of the person. A duty with an
unrecorded end is still running or was never closed in the roster.", "fields": {"volunteer": "Marcus Oyelaran", "base": "Ravenscar Hut", "duty": "warden", "stretch": {"begins_ms": "2024-03-16"}}, "relation": "Marcus Oyelaran serves as warden at Ravenscar Hut"}
{"record_kind": "BaseDuty", "meaning": "A volunteer's duty at a base over an interval. `duty` is the capacity
they served in then, not a lasting trait of the person. A duty with an
unrecorded end is still running or was never closed in the roster.", "fields": {"volunteer": "Marcus Oyelaran", "base": "Cragfoot Store", "duty": "medic", "stretch": {"begins_ms": "2023-12-27"}}, "relation": "Marcus Oyelaran serves as medic at Cragfoot Store"}
{"record_kind": "Crag", "meaning": "A named feature of the fell such as a gully, ridge or scree slope,
mentioned by the name walkers use. Names are not unique keys. An
unrecorded elevation means nobody has fixed it with a GPS reading.", "fields": {"name": "Black Scar"}}
{"record_kind": "Callout", "meaning": "One call-out to a casualty on the fell. `incident_lead` directs the
search from the control vehicle and `field_commander` leads the party
on the ground; they may be the same member or different ones. An
unrecorded stand-down date means the call-out has not been closed. An
unrecorded crag means the casualty was never placed on a named feature.
An unrecorded search time means nobody kept a log of it.", "fields": {"title": "Walker with ankle injury below Nightjar Edge", "incident_lead": "Priya Raghunathan", "field_commander": "Marcus Oyelaran", "crag": "Grey Mare Scree", "raised_at": "2025-04-19", "stood_down_on": "2025-09-15", "search_minutes": "240 minutes", "recovery_cost": {"cents": 62500, "currency": "ZAR"}}}
{"record_kind": "Callout", "meaning": "One call-out to a casualty on the fell. `incident_lead` directs the
search from the control vehicle and `field_commander` leads the party
on the ground; they may be the same member or different ones. An
unrecorded stand-down date means the call-out has not been closed. An
unrecorded crag means the casualty was never placed on a named feature.
An unrecorded search time means nobody kept a log of it.", "fields": {"title": "Fell runner collapsed near Harrow Tarn", "incident_lead": "Marcus Oyelaran", "field_commander": "Hannah Birkett", "crag": "Nightjar Gully", "raised_at": "2025-11-29", "stood_down_on": "2025-07-12", "search_minutes": "270 minutes", "recovery_cost": {"cents": 101500, "currency": "NZD"}}}
{"record_kind": "Outfitter", "meaning": "A shop or maker that sells gear to the team. Names are not unique
keys; one shop may trade under several banners.", "fields": {"name": "Greta Hollow Sports", "banners": ["Scafell Gear Shed", "Borrowdale Bivouac", "Kirkstone Trading"]}}
